            "review_title": "Review at Com Tam Ba Son",
            "review_text": "kvinh2013\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam175 contributions\n1\nIt's all Good for the Hood\nMay 2015 • Solo\nI passed by this neighborhood restaurant a few time before I came in to order the quintessential Com Tam; which is a grilled pork chop on a bed of broken rice, julienne pork skin, pate, pickled radish and carrot and the whole mound doused generously with a diluted concoction of fish sauce and chili. In the order of importance: the pork chop is of a good size and quality, the grilling and marinade gave it the signature flame licked meat, however, like most food in VN, it is a bit on the sweet side for me, the julienne pork have a genuine taste to it. This is a remarkable achievement considering all the revolting stories about Franken-julienne-pork meat we read in the media in VN. The broken rice is done right, the pickles ought to be julienne to conform to the traditional formula. On the universal scale for Com Tam this plate at 4 bucks comes in at number 8. With a fleet of motorcycles out front ready to deliver this is a welcome addition to the neighborhood.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten May 24, 2015",
